[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked **known: one issue, one fix queued**. It is not one issue.
The desk merged on subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)), and
reports with the same subject came from three different bugs. The queued parser fix closes only
the first one.

<Callout kind="warn">
Do not close #4471 when the parser fix ships. Each problem below has its own ticket and its own fix.
</Callout>

## The split

<ProblemSplit ticket={4471} {tickets} />

## The three problems

**`parser`: dates read month first.** The shared parser reads every date month first. All our
tenants write the day first, so any date with a day of 12 or less comes out with day and month
swapped: 2 March becomes 3 February. Comes in through the app, by email and through
booking-v2's form. This is the fix that is queued.

**`hint`: booking-v3's date hint says `MM/DD/YYYY`.** booking-v3's form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under
its date field, but reads what people type the tenant's way, day first. People follow the hint,
so their dates flip even after the parser is fixed. Only form reports from booking-v3 tenants.
The fix is in the form: the hint must match the tenant's locale.

**`shift`: the date moves by one day.** These reports are not a swap at all: Tuesday shows as
Monday, an invite arrives before the booking was made, a client in Lisbon and a client in Toronto
got different days for the same meeting, every booking in June is one day off. The desk already
noted them as a one-day move (`desk-notes.json`), then filed them under `parser` by tenant. It
looks like a time-zone or daylight-saving conversion, and the parser fix will not touch it.

## How the reports were placed

- One report per id: the export pages overlap, so repeats are counted once (`uniqueById`).
- The tenant decides, not intake's tag: `meta.intakeTag` is a guess from the reporter's browser
  and disagrees with the tenant often.
- A report on the desk's one-day-move list is `shift`; every other report gets its cause from
  `causes.ts` (tenant locale and booking form).

For comparison, the table on #4471 today, which counts the one-day moves under `parser`:

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## What to change

- Track each problem on its own ticket; close #4471 only when all three are closed.
- Subject lines say what people saw, not what broke. Decision 0001 needs a successor that checks
  the tenant and the channel before a merge.

